e; no UI changes are expected\n51\t  beyond any value shown for the default.\n52\t- No changes to activity detection (kernel probe behavior) or per-project /\n53\t  per-user culling policies — out of scope per the strategy.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- A freshly installed cluster with no admin configuration applies a workbench\n58\t  idle culling timeout of 8 hours (was 24).\n59\t- Upgrading a cluster whose idle culling timeout was explicitly configured\n60\t  leaves the explicit value unchanged.\n61\t- A cluster without an explicitly configured value uses the 8-hour default\n62\t  after upgrade.\n63\t- An admin can still view and override the timeout through the existing\n64\t  Dashboard administration UI, and the override takes precedence over the\n65\t  default.\n66\t- Idle culling behavior is otherwise unchanged (activity detection semantics\n67\t  untouched).\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t- HLR-1 (P1): The default idle culling timeout for newly installed clusters\n72\t  is 8 hours instead of 24; existing clusters with an explicitly configured\n73\t  value are not changed on upgrade.\n74\t\n75\t## Notes\n76\t\n77\t- The change is a default-value flip in existing configuration handling; it\n78\t  is revertible by restoring the prior default, and explicitly configured\n79\t  clusters are never touched.\n80\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b18495991746d856","agent_id":"ab7dbf8ff1f6919c9","session_id":"ba0e710c-819a-4430-9b1f-ad9788382ed4","uuid":"38aac177-d525-4ec2-b20b-e0d5b497ba9e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T17:33:47.450Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-94ab98819dee4f47","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9003 decomposition"}
